[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Open Games (1...e5)"]
[Variation "Scotch Game: Classical Variation"]
[ECO "C45"]
[Character "positional,tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "bishop-hits-knight,central-pawns"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "3.d4 exd4 4.Nxd4"]
[Start "giuoco-piano 2...Nc6"]

3. d4 { White opens the centre at once. } 3... exd4 { Take it: the pawn on d4 is not defended. } 4. Nxd4 ( 4. Ng5 h6 { The knight has nothing to attack on g5, so Black asks it to leave. } 5. Nf3 Nf6 ) 4... Bc5 { Develops with an attack on the knight on d4. } 5. Be3 ( 5. Nxc6 Qf6 { Attacks the knight on c6 and the pawn on f2 together. } 6. Qd2 ( 6. Qf3 dxc6 ) ( 6. f3 dxc6 ) ( 6. Qe2 dxc6 ) ( 6. Be3 Bxe3 { Removes the bishop first; after fxe3 White's pawns are doubled and the king's side is loose. } 7. fxe3 dxc6 ) 6... dxc6 7. Nc3 Be6 ) ( 5. Nb3 Bb6 6. Nc3 Nf6 ) ( 5. c3 Nf6 { Develops with an attack on e4. The pawn on c3 has taken the knight's best square. } 6. Nxc6 bxc6 ) 5... Qf6 { Attacks the knight on d4 a second time. The queen is exposed, but White must keep defending the knight. } 6. c3 { Defends the knight on d4 with a pawn. } ( 6. Nxc6 Bxe3 7. fxe3 dxc6 { Recaptures toward the centre and opens the c8 bishop. White's doubled e-pawns are a lasting weakness. } ) 6... Nge7 { Develops a knight without blocking the queen, and prepares to castle. } 7. Bc4 O-O { Castle: the king is safe and the rook joins in. } 8. O-O Bb6 { Steps back before Nb3 can hit it, and still aims at d4. Plan: ...d6, ...Ne5 and ...Bf5. } *
